  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the weight of Samantha's watermelon to the nearest ten:\n\n$$\n12⟶10\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the weight of Samantha's watermelon to the weight of Harry's watermelon is \n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the weight of Samantha's  watermelon and the denominator represents  the weight of Harry's watermelon.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $10$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 2}{3\\times 2}=\\frac{10}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Harry's watermelon approximately weighs $6$ kilograms.",
